Subject: [PATCH] tls: add optional NSS AES-GCM and registered-buffer batching

Keep CPU TLS as the default. Provide cryptodev and optional persistent CMA
backends for Go TLS and uTLS, with borrowed RX batches and direct ready TCP
input. Isolated overlays leave the shared Go SDK and module cache untouched.
Include regression tests for authentication, ownership and concurrent close.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

--- a/_nss/README.md
+++ b/_nss/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Optional NSS TLS backend
+
+These files are build inputs for overlay.py, not a Go package. The overlay
+patches an isolated copy of uTLS and selected Go/Xray files without modifying
+the shared Go SDK or module cache. NSS is built only when XRAY_CORE_NSS_TLS=y
+on IPQ60xx/IPQ807x; ordinary CPU TLS remains the runtime default.
+
+Runtime selection:
+
+- XRAY_NSS_TLS=cryptodev: NSS CryptoAPI via /dev/crypto.
+- XRAY_NSS_TLS=dmabuf: optional /dev/nss-crypto-dmabuf registered CMA path.
+- XRAY_NSS_TLS=cpu-batch: CPU AES-GCM control using the same batch pipeline.
+- XRAY_NSS_TLS=cpu (or unset): ordinary CPU TLS.
+
+The DMA-BUF path requires the matching optional kernel driver and private CMA
+pool; rebuild the kernel and all modules together. It is experimental and has
+AX5/IPQ6000 runtime validation; IPQ807x has build validation only.
+
+For the tested throughput path, also set XRAY_NSS_READ_BORROW=1 and
+XRAY_NSS_TX_DIRECT=1. Borrowing passes authenticated mapped output to Xray and
+releases a batch when its last Buffer is released. Consumers must release the
+previous batch before requesting another batch on the same TLS connection.
+Close cancels waiting reads but retains memory still held by a consumer.
+The optional XRAY_NSS_BORROW_NOTIFY=cond replaces per-batch channels; channels
+remain the default. XRAY_NSS_READ_BATCH=1 selects the older copying RX batch
+path and is superseded by READ_BORROW. All these paths remain opt-in.
+
+Direct TX reads already-ready plain TCP data into mapped TLS input slots and
+batches encryption and socket writes. It never waits on the input socket while
+holding the TLS output lock. Unsupported/transforming wrappers and not-ready
+reads fall back to ordinary Copy. Both paths remove userspace copies, not the
+socket kernel copy. No asynchronous multi-bank pipeline is provided.
+
+XRAY_NSS_DMA_BATCH=1..16 bounds the slot count (default 16). Batches use only
+already-available records and never wait to fill. The CPU-batch control opens
+no NSS device. XRAY_NSS_TLS_VERIFY=1 enables CPU cross-checking for diagnostics;
+disable it when measuring throughput. Cryptodev rejects requests beyond the
+verified hardware length limit and retains software fallback.
+
+Tests cover TLS 1.2/1.3, uTLS, corrupted records, traffic-key changes, buffer
+ownership, close/reuse races, dynamic record sizing, direct read deadlines and
+accounting, and handshake state changes while acquiring the output lock.
+Generate the overlay with the package Go environment, then use go test -race
+with -overlay=<dest>/overlay.json and -modfile=<dest>/go.mod for crypto/tls,
+github.com/refraction-networking/utls, ./common/buf and ./transport/internet/tls
+with -run NSS. Linux/ARM64 device tests additionally need the matching driver.
